-e16f24627bd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s>{s}_{0}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331791/field-4/48b411620ed377ee9222b817c8ed23aa5c39bdb48880d81d507d29eeec3ddf84" :answer/id #uuid "234d4b48-9c83-5334-a0b7-a5c6a1b63dbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s>{s}_{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331791/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f88dc181-63a3-5f9a-88b9-430acd88ac69" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-331791/field-4/6fbda98753f2c3b7cf5ca67cfd6b814821d1773abd6d09e2219d8239acb9592b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331791/field-4/6fbda98753f2c3b7cf5ca67cfd6b814821d1773abd6d09e2219d8239acb9592b" "q-331791/field-4/275fc4b635e1f6c5b5be4f40d628f3b447495354590878c45588707815582cc4" "q-331791/field-4/48b411620ed377ee9222b817c8ed23aa5c39bdb48880d81d507d29eeec3ddf84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331791" :question/id #uuid "65e33f37-ed72-5eab-bd4d-b7d3ad4f22b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-331791" :question/problem "Consider a function $y(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{y(t)}=Y(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{4t}y(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.By definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}y(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}y(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $Y(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=Y(s-4),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-4>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331791/field-1" "q-331791/field-2" "q-331791/field-3" "q-331791/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeb2589b-0135-5bbb-bc91-ec121ee5defd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331798/field-1/6787fe96b798a6321a93ab84dc5fadb900e9e2d852f35d53e71b9320ebfa8845" :answer/id #uuid "08b9b970-b7b7-59c5-92f5-1342eace5cea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{8t}m(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331798/field-1/b60fe2da9a53cac6542549a74ca0d8804d85625380e816bfcf50909fa7257c0e" :answer/id #uuid "c90ae389-f230-5149-a38a-097cae319adf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{8t}m(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331798/field-1/9e99bf3219788fd9540e491d90c84c0b29b4a828c980fc7c6ae9860d7140ca12" :answer/id #uuid "7f52864a-a328-5c19-a6ce-173f6a6f1893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-8t}m(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331798/field-1/a0047c05d90fcd5e0c9b637f7c8b89d6b8006b3c70b447a7ba0fc45671a07657" :answer/id #uuid "440dcd46-2a2a-57c3-8530-df74c65be9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{-8t}m(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331798/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a48df3-d481-58fe-b519-c12bca6d7071" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-331798/field-1/9e99bf3219788fd9540e491d90c84c0b29b4a828c980fc7c6ae9860d7140ca12" :answer-field/choices ["q-331798/field-1/6787fe96b798a6321a93ab84dc5fadb900e9e2d852f35d53e71b9320ebfa8845" "q-331798/field-1/b60fe2da9a53cac6542549a74ca0d8804d85625380e816bfcf50909fa7257c0e" "q-331798/field-1/9e99bf3219788fd9540e491d90c84c0b29b4a828c980fc7c6ae9860d7140ca12" "q-331798/field-1/a0047c05d90fcd5e0c9b637f7c8b89d6b8006b